===============================================================================
4. Maintenance Grant
===============================================================================

The Work is considered “broken” if, on the latest public stable version of
Captain of Industry®, it:

- cannot be loaded,
- crashes the Game,
- corrupts or prevents normal use of saves, or
- otherwise fails in a way that substantially prevents players from using the
  Work as intended.

If the Work remains broken for at least ten (10) days, it becomes eligible for
community maintenance unless, during that period, the Licensor has published
either:

- an update, or
- a Maintenance Notice.

===============================================================================
5. Maintenance Notice
===============================================================================

A “Maintenance Notice” means a public statement by the Licensor, posted on the
Hub, the Work’s repository, or another official project page, stating that the
Licensor is aware that the Work is broken and intends to update it.

A Maintenance Notice prevents community maintenance only until thirty (30) days
after the Work first became broken.

If the Work remains broken after that thirty (30) day period, it becomes
eligible for community maintenance even if a Maintenance Notice was posted.

===============================================================================
6. Community Maintenance Rights
===============================================================================

Once the Work is eligible for community maintenance, any person may:

(a) modify the Work only as reasonably necessary to:
    - fix issues,
    - restore compatibility with the Game, or
    - fix bugs;

(b) distribute the modified Work as a clearly labeled
    "Community Maintenance Release"; and

(c) continue these activities for as long as the original Work would otherwise
    remain broken.

===============================================================================
7. Limitations of the Maintenance Grant
===============================================================================

This grant is limited strictly to maintenance purposes.

It does NOT authorize:

- adding unrelated new features,
- removal of Licensor attribution,
- redistribution as a standalone asset pack, or
- incorporation into another software product, game, or interactive media
  product.

===============================================================================
8. End of Maintenance Grant
===============================================================================

If the Licensor later publishes an update that fixes the broken Work, the
Maintenance Grant ends for future updates to community maintenance releases,
unless the Work later becomes eligible for community maintenance again.

Community maintenance releases already created in good faith may continue to
exist.

